0,Olumarama Language (LRM) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/lrm/,"Olumarama is a stable indigenous language of Kenya. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family and is part of the Oluluyia macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Olumarama,Niger-Congo
1,(PDF) the phonological processes in olumarama: NC effects and...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/355425294_THE_PHONOLOGICAL_PROCESSES_IN_OLUMARAMA_NC_EFFECTS_AND_VOWEL_HIATUS,"the voicing of the consonants. Olumarama, just like many Niger-Congo languages (Casali, 1996) has a five. vowel system derived from the Proto-Bantu seven vowel system (Hombert &. Hyman, 1999).",Olumarama,Niger-Congo
